  "domain": "IoT / Smart Home",
  "statement": "Design an object-oriented model for a smart home hub. A SmartHub manages a collection of independent SmartDevice objects (which can be paired or unpaired without destroying the devices). Both Thermostat and SmartLock inherit from the abstract SmartDevice class, which declares a turnOn() / getStatus() contract.",
  "deliverables": [
    "Model SmartHub, an abstract SmartDevice class, Thermostat, and SmartLock.",
    "Use Generalization for Thermostat and SmartLock inheriting from SmartDevice.",
    "Use Aggregation from SmartHub to SmartDevice since devices exist independently of the hub."
  ],
  "hints": [
    "Mark SmartDevice as an abstract class in the Inspector.",
    "Thermostat -> SmartDevice and SmartLock -> SmartDevice use Generalization.",
    "SmartHub -> SmartDevice uses Aggregation (hollow diamond) because devices survive if the hub is replaced."
  ],
